WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.297
A common table expression is a temporary named result inside one S Q L statement.

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:09.807
Think of it as giving a name to an intermediate step.

00:00:09.807 --> 00:00:12.427
One step might filter patients.

00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:15.112
Another step might count admissions.

00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:20.191
A later step can use that prepared result instead of repeating the same logic.

00:00:20.656 --> 00:00:25.493
The important point is that the common table expression is not a permanent table.

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:28.643
It exists only while that statement runs.

00:00:28.643 --> 00:00:36.668
When you see a long query, try reading it as a sequence of small named stages instead of one large block of code.
